[IntendedResult "win"]

{ An outside passed pawn pulls his king away from the real battle. Watch the capture, then create yours. } 2... bxa5 { He takes the a pawn. Recapture with your b pawn to make an outside passed pawn. [%cal Yb4a5] } 3. bxa5 { Your outside passed pawn distracts his king on the queenside, so your own king is free to head for g5 and h6. [%tail] [%cal Gf3e4,Gb4a5] } (3. b5 { That loses: b5 avoids the trade, but nothing is left to stop his a pawn once it runs. } 3... a4 4. bxc6 4... Kd6 { His a pawn runs free this way. Recapture on a5 before any new pawn race. [%cal Re6d6] }) (3. c5 { That loses too: c5 ignores the a pawn entirely, and Black simply pushes his outside passer toward promotion. } 3... a4 { He pushes the outside passer instead of taking b4. Your king cannot catch it. } 4. Ke4 4... a3 { This lets the a pawn run free. Take on a5 first, before racing pawns. [%cal Ra4a3] }) (3. Ke4 { That loses: e4 skips the recapture, and axb4 leaves you down a pawn with no outside passer to show for it. } 3... axb4 4. Kd4 4... Ke7 { You lose the b pawn instead of making a passer. Recapture on a5. [%cal Re6e7] }) 3... Kd6 4. Ke4 4... Kc5 5. Kf5 5... Kd4 6. a6 6... Ke3 7. a7 7... Kd4 8. a8=Q { Queen! Your outside passed pawn promoted while his king was still stuck in the middle. [%csl Ga8] } 1-0


[Event "Lasker endgames: Win the race back to the other wing"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/8/p4k2/1p5p/1P3P1K/P7/8/8_b_-_-_1_6"]
[White "Opponent"]
[Black "Student"]
