[Role "exercise"]
[Block "Stalemate resources"]
[Source "Edward Lasker, Chess Strategy (1915); Part I, Chapter V, queen versus pawn, case B"]
[Verification "Stockfish 18 NNUE checked; see accompanying report"]
[IntendedResult "draw"]

{ You are down to a king and a pawn against his queen, but that pawn is one step from promoting: find the stalemate shelter after the check. } 1... Qb6+ { The queen checks from b6. Which corner square leaves your king with nothing to do? } 2. Ka8 { Your king tucks into the corner. If the queen takes the pawn on c7 now, your king has no move at all. [%cal Gb8a8] } (2. Kc8 { That loses: blocking your own pawn on c8 gives up the stalemate trick before it even starts. } 2... Kd5 3. Kd7 3... Qd6+ 4. Ke8 4... Qxc7 { Black wins your pawn. Without it, your king cannot hold against the queen. [%cal Rd6c7] }) 2... Qc6+ { He checks from c6 rather than grabbing the pawn outright. Only one corner square keeps your trap alive. } 3. Kb8 { His queen covers a8 along the diagonal, so b8 it is, and there your own king guards the pawn on c7. [%cal Ga8b8] } (3. Ka7 { That steps out of the shelter and drops the pawn. } 3... Qxc7+ 4. Ka8 4... Qd7 { The pawn is gone, the check killed the stalemate, and his queen will run your bare king down. You are lost. [%csl Ra8] }) 3... Qb6+ { He checks once more from b6, hoping you step the wrong way. } 4. Ka8 { Back in the corner on a8, and the pawn on c7 is poison: the moment his queen takes it your king has no legal move. Drawn. [%csl Ga8] } (4. Kc8 { Out of the corner, and the pawn loses its shelter. } 4... Kd5 5. Kd7 5... Qd6+ 6. Ke8 6... Qxc7 { His king walked straight in and took the pawn on c7. With nothing left to hide behind, you are lost. [%csl Rc7] }) 1-0


[Event "Lasker endgames: Keep the king trapped on the rook file"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/8/K7/8/8/3k4/P7/8_b_-_-_0_1"]
[White "Opponent"]
[Black "Student"]
[Result "0-1"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/0N4zuDFR/vNlGwv0k"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/K7/8/8/3k4/P7/8 b - - 0 1"]
[ChapterId "E17"]
[Domain "endgame"]
[Role "teaching"]
[Block "Rook-pawn fortresses"]
[Source "Edward Lasker, Chess Strategy (1915); Part I, Chapter V, Diagram 55"]
